    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I know, I know. You're just supposed to say that. But it's not like a phone call changes the fact that everything is already destroyed. It's just a cycle of trying to fix things that are fundamentally broken beyond repair. Sometimes, when everything is this quiet and this empty, it feels like the only honest thing left to do is just accept the end. Like it's just a natural conclusion to a story that's already over.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
